he Carrión river in the province of Palencia, Castile and León.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/carrowmore"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/carrowmore.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Carrowmore</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Carrowmore is a large cemetery of megalithic tombs on the Cúil Irra peninsula near Sligo in north-west Ireland.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/carta-de-logu"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/carta-de-logu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Carta de Logu</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Carta de Logu is a law code issued in the Sardinian language by Eleanor of Arborea in 1392, revising an earlier code of her father Marianus IV.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/cartagena-manifesto"><span class="enc-name">Cartagena Manifesto</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Cartagena Manifesto is a political statement written by Simón Bolívar in Cartagena de Indias in December 1812, after the fall of the First Republic of Venezuela.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cartagena-colombia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/cartagena-colombia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cartagena, Colombia</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Cartagena de Indias is a port city on the Caribbean coast of Colombia, founded by Pedro de Heredia in 1533.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/cartago-costa-rica"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/cartago-costa-rica.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cartago, Costa Rica</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class