s="enc-snip">Cassivellaunus was a British war leader who led the resistance to Julius Caesar's second invasion of Britain in 54 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/caste"><span class="enc-name">Caste</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">Caste refers to a system of hereditary social groups, often tied to occupation and restricting marriage between groups.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/caste-war-of-yucatan"><span class="enc-name">Caste War of Yucatán</span><span class="enc-type">War · Revolt · 1847–1901</span><span class="enc-snip">The Caste War of Yucatán was a long uprising of the Maya against the Hispanic and mestizo elites of the Yucatán Peninsula.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/castel-di-castro"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/castel-di-castro.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Castel di Castro</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Castel di Castro is the fortified hilltop quarter of Cagliari in Sardinia, built by the Pisans from 1216 with the reluctant consent of Judge Benedetta of Cagliari.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/castel-nuovo"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/castel-nuovo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Castel Nuovo</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Castel Nuovo is a castle on the harbour of Naples, begun in 1279 by Charles I of Anjou when he moved the capital from Palermo.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/castel-santangelo"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/castel-santangelo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Castel Sant'Angelo</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">Castel Sant'Angelo is a fortress in Rome on the right bank of the Tiber, built in the second century as the mausoleum of the emperor Hadrian.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/castell-bank"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/castell-bank.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Castell Bank</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The Castell Bank was founded in 1774 by the counts of Castell in Franconia to manage the finances of their small county and lend to its subjects.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/castell-dinas-bran"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/castell-dinas-bran.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Castell Dinas Brân</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">Castell Dinas Brân is a ruined medieval castle on a steep hill above Llangollen in north-east Wales.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/castell-y-bere"><span class="enc-name">Castell y Bere</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">Castell y Bere is a ruined Welsh castle in Gwynedd, north-west Wales, built by Llywelyn the Great from about 1221 to secure the southern border of his lands.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/castello-d-empuries"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/castello-d-empuries.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Castelló d'Empúries</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Castelló d'Empúries is a town in the Alt Empordà in north-eastern Catalonia, near the Gulf of Roses.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/castelvecchio-verona"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/castelvecchio-verona.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Castelvecchio (Verona)</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">Castelvecchio is a fortress in Verona built from 1354 by Cangrande II della Scala, together with the fortified Ponte Scaligero across the Adige.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/castiglione-delle-stiviere"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/castiglione-delle-stiviere.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Castiglione delle Stiviere</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Castiglione delle Stiviere is a town in the province of Mantua in Lombardy, Italy, south of Lake Garda.</span></a></li></ul>
